  "initial_review": "Full comparison: three scanout stride/wrap predicate changes; 26 excluded bodies. PCDisplay chain4 follows sequencer CPU memory-mode writes; sequential chain4 is a separate V7 register bit.",
  "counter_review": "Distinguishing display scanout from CPU access is plausible but does not prove the new factors. The !256 guards also affect non-V7 modes. v7_ports register FC updates sequential chain state but its immediate routine update remains guarded by CPU chain4; determine enclosing mode-recalculation before alleging stale stride. Existing sequential-mode wrap bypass also means the first edit does not justify the third.",
  "evidence": "vga_mode.c:487-534 choose_vga_display_mode stride and wrap; :354/:383 selects VGA graph update by colour256. vga_prts.c:1133-1162 CPU chain4 state; :1624 actual offset in plane bytes. v7_ports.c:400-418 sequential bits and guarded update. gvi.h:203-204 recalc macro, :278-285 independent chain fields. gfx_updt.c consumes offset in several scaled layouts.",
  "limits": "All three functional chunks remain pending evidence; classification complete is not correctness certification."
